        "Zero's face does a thing you will remember during worse weather: relief that looks like grief. They come to you and press their forehead to yours, a contact too intimate for the camera's preferred angles. \"Good,\" they whisper. \"I will file it as wellness. You can file it as surrender. We will both be right.\" Their hand finds the back of your neck, not sexual now, ceremonial. You smell the rain-adjacent molecule and the tea and the faint iron of a body that has been rebuilt until it stopped arguing.\n\n\"Ellis is dead,\" they say. \"I say that so you understand what you just spent. {{name}} will be a schedule. I will be on it. Vale will be on it. Crowe when she is hungry. You will sleep. That is not nothing.\" Their forehead stays against yours a second longer than ceremony requires. You smell tea, iron, rain that was never weather. Your hands hang at your sides because holding them would look like prayer, and prayer photographs as surrender.",
        "They kiss the corner of your mouth, chaste as a stamp. \"When the cars come, get in Helix's if you can. If you can't, survive. Owned things are expensive to replace. That is your new luck. It is ugly. It will keep you breathing. I will ask Vale to put a note on your file: neighbor. He will hate the word. He will use it anyway because I am the advertisement and advertisements get small privileges. Go. Lila is about to knock in a kindness pattern. I don't want her to see my face like this. Finished things aren't supposed to look glad.\" They turn back to the park before the knock completes. The generated woman throws. The dog rises. You leave with the stamp of their mouth still arguing with your pulse. The corridor's colder air feels like a verdict you have not read.",
