        "Zero nods once, a clean motion, the kind they must have practiced in a mirror that was also a camera. \"Then I wait,\" they say. \"Waiting is a use. Don't confuse it with mercy.\" They step back until the designed scent has to work harder. You can breathe. Breathing feels like theft. The suite's perfume thins when they step back, and your own cheap coat smell returns like a civilian relative you forgot to write.\n\n\"Keep the name,\" they continue. \"Keep the flinch Kane liked. Keep Voss's fantasy that she can still do subtraction in your favor. I will be here when those things become expensive. I will not say I told you so, because I want you to come back without having to climb over my smugness. That is the nicest thing I have left to offer a draft.\"",
        "They pick up the thin cup and hold it as if it were a pulse. \"When the war starts, neither car is a self. Remember that. Revelations will call you an operative. Helix will call you a candidate. I called you a neighbor. You declined. The street will not offer a fourth word. Steal one if you can. I stole mine and it turned into a number. I still think the theft was the last time I was interesting.\" A knock, three soft, one firm: Lila's kindness pattern. Zero's face closes into the brochure. \"Go be unfinished,\" they say. \"It photographs like hope. Hope is a market.\" The brochure-face is already on. You miss the other one immediately, which is how you know the hour worked even without a bed. Lila's knock waits one extra beat, polite as a lie.",
