        "Zero's smile is the first one that looks like Ellis. It is not kind. It is impressed, which is worse. \"A double,\" they say. \"That's how I lasted. That's how I lost. You will tell Voss you are hers. You will tell Crowe you are a good investment. You will tell me you might stay. I will pretend to believe you because pretending is a form of touch I am still allowed.\" The generated park stays paused. The dog hangs. You understand the pause as a courtesy and as a threat. Both can be true in a room this well lit.\n\nThey come close enough to put two fingers on your pulse again. It jumps. They let it. \"Doubles die of scheduling,\" they say. \"Or they live long enough to become me. I will not stop you. I will keep a room. If both firms burn you, the room is still here. That is not loyalty. That is inventory with a pulse. Don't thank me.\"",
        "The knock comes. Zero does not step back. \"Kane will appear when the shooting starts,\" they say, quickly, a gift that might be bait. \"He always does. He looks like billing and he is a knife. If you get in his car, he will ask you to burn someone. If you get in Helix's, Radek will do the same with worse vocabulary. Burn someone who isn't me. I am tired of being the easy sacrifice. Ellis was easy. I am not Ellis. Neither are you, not after this hour. Now put your liaison face on. Vale can smell a double if you leave it on the skin.\" Their fingers leave your pulse. The jump stays. You put the liaison face on like a coat that has begun to fit too well, and you hate the fit in a way that might still be useful.",
